# PART 1 — Live on-chain data

Several figures currently update only on page load, some go stale silently, and
some still read "needs indexer". Fix all of it.

## 1.1 — Source map first

Before writing anything, produce a table of every figure the app displays: its
source, its refresh behaviour, and what it does when that source fails.
**Report this to me before making changes.**

Intended sources:

| Figure | Source |
|---|---|
| Price | On-chain, StateView `getSlot0` |
| Backing per token | On-chain, BackingLens |
| Total ballast | On-chain, summed across projects |
| Launches | On-chain, factory registry union |
| Holder count and list | Blockscout |
| 24h volume, change, OHLCV | GeckoTerminal |
| Recent trades | GeckoTerminal |
| Fees accrued and claimed | On-chain, hook ledger |
| Burns | On-chain, from Part 2 |

Anything not in that table either has no source or is derived from these. Say
which.

## 1.2 — Refresh behaviour

- **On-chain reads** every 12 seconds, and immediately after any transaction
  the user sends.
- **Blockscout and GeckoTerminal** every 30 seconds through the existing
  server-side proxies, cached so a hundred viewers cause one upstream call.
- **Recent trades** append new rows rather than replacing the list, so the feed
  reads as live rather than as a page that reloaded.
- Refresh pauses when the tab is hidden, resumes on focus. Do not burn RPC
  quota on background tabs.

Every figure carries a freshness indicator: a small dot and a relative
timestamp. "Live", "delayed 2m", or "unavailable". Never a number with no
indication of when it was true.

## 1.3 — Degrade honestly

This matters more than the refresh rate.

- Source unreachable → "unavailable". Never a zero, never the last value
  presented as current.
- Source lagging → show the value with "delayed" and its actual age.
- External source disagrees with chain by more than 1% → the chain governs, and
  say so. This already happens on the token page; apply it everywhere.
- Never silently substitute one source for another.

## 1.4 — Reconciliation

Every figure must agree everywhere it appears. Same source, no separate
counters, no cached totals that drift.

- Analytics totals equal the sum of what Discover lists
- A token's market cap is identical on Discover, its token page, and in a
  portfolio row
- Holder count equals the length of the holder list
- 24h volume equals the sum of the trades feed over that window

Add a development-only console check that flags any mismatch. If two paths can
disagree, eventually they will.

## 1.5 — Remaining "needs indexer" labels

Report which figures still show that. For each: source it from Blockscout or
GeckoTerminal, or state honestly why it cannot be sourced.

Portfolio cost basis stays absent. It cannot be reconstructed from public data
without guessing, and a wrong P&L is worse than none. Keep the explanation
visible on the page.

## 1.6 — On Dune

I am willing to build Dune dashboards if they add something.

Investigate and recommend: does Dune index chain 4663, and would it give us
